  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conflict-Affected Populations Fleeing Ukraine to Poland Have Increased Access to Multisector Humanitarian Assistance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The war in Ukraine has triggered one of the largest humanitarian crises on record with over 7.7 million people displaced in the country and another 5 million refugees and 224,000 third country nationals fleeing across borders. As the crisis continues to evolve, displacement patterns continue to change. Flexibility to support previously trapped populations in newly accessible areas, and to address new and secondary displacements and returning populations with humanitarian assistance, remains at the forefront of the response. The overarching goal of this project is that conflict-affected populations fleeing Ukraine to Poland have increased access to multisector humanitarian assistance. Through this project, IOM is implementing a multi-sector humanitarian response, supporting Government partners and local authorities to respond through provision of shelter, multi-purpose cash, and support to municipalities for schools to facilitate inclusion of newly arrived students.</narrative>
  </description>
